--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                       CODING RULES FOR stdlib_*.asm FILES
                 for automatic generation of the dependency file
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1) CODE STRUCTURE FOR A GENERIC Routine(i):

!ifdef caml_PRIM__<ROUTINE_LBL(i)> {
     ;; -- OR --
!ifdef caml_AUX__<ROUTINE_LBL(i)> {
  
<ROUTINE_LBL(i)>
    ... <acme_code> ...
[ <GLOB_SYM(i,1)> [ = <acme_expr> ]]
    ... <acme_code> ...
[ <GLOB_SYM(i,n)> [ = <acme_expr> ]]
    ... <acme_code> ...
    [ <FALLTHROUGH_COMMENT> ]   <--- MANDATORY FOR FALLTHROUGH POINTS
}                               <--- MUST BE IN 1ST COLUMN


* <ROUTINE_LBL(i)> ::= caml_<NAME>
  The label for the entry point of Routine(i).      E.g. caml_load_1st_arg

* <GLOB_SYM(i,x)> ::= <ROUTINE_LBL(i)>__<NAME>
  The x-th global symbol defined in Routine(i).     E.g. caml_load_1st_arg__addr
  Note the TWO underscores before <NAME>.

* <NAME> ::= [a-zA-Z](_?[a-zA-Z0-9])*
  One or more alnum strings, separated by ONE       E.g. load_1sr_arg
  underscore; the 1st character must be a letter.

* <FALLTHROUGH_COMMENT> ::= ;+[ \t]+fallthrough[ \t]+<ROUTINE_LBL(i+1)>
  Comment for a fallthrough point to Routine(i+1).  E.g. ;Fallthrough caml_next
  The "fallthrough" word is case-insensitive.

* The final closing curly brace must be in the FIRST COLUMN; no other '}' within
  <acme_code> may be in the first column.

* If a fallthrough point is present, it MUST be commented out with a
  <FALLTHROUGH_COMMENT>; the comment must PRECEDE the final closing '}'.

* DO NOT refer, within <acme_code> or <acme_expr> of Routine(i)>, to zone-local
  symbols (labels beginning with '.') defined in another Routine(j), or to
  global symbols that do not conform to the definition of <GLOB_SYM(j,_)>.

* All characters from the leftmost ';' to the end of the line will be treated as
  comments and ignored, even if the ';' is enclosed in single or double quotes:

  BAD:   LDA #';':JSR caml_my_routine  ;this dependency WILL NOT BE DETECTED!
  GOOD:  LDA #';'
         JSR caml_my_routine           ;this dependency will be detected.


2) HOW DEPENDENCIES ARE DETECTED BY mkdepends:

 * Any occurrence of <ROUTINE_LBL(j)> or <GLOB_SYM(j,_)> in <acme_code> or
   <acme_expr> within Routine(i) will be treated as a dependency of Routine(i)
   on Routine(j), j <> i.

 * A <FALLTHROUGH_COMMENT> will be treated as a dependency of Routine(i) on
   Routine(i+1).

 * After identifying the set of all dependencies, the script calculates its
   transitive closure and generates the file with required symbol assignments.
